<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coro, Venezuela</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Santa Ana de Coro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coro, formally Santa Ana de Coro, is a city in north-western Venezuela, the capital of Falcón state. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-ampies">Juan de Ampíes</a> in 1527, it is one of the oldest Spanish towns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> and was the first capital of the province of Venezuela and the base of the Welser colony. Its colonial centre and port of La Vela, with houses built of earth, are a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coro-venezuela.jpg" alt="Coro, Venezuela" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luisontiveros · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casco_central_Santa_Ana_de_Coro,_estado_Falcon,_Venezuela.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
